{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified VAI 12 days before the posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D7"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the rocuronium bromide shortage on 2023-02-15 and it remains current as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["E44", "D9"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hikma Farmaceutica (Portugal) plant that manufactures the Hikma-labeled vials used at Corvale East, Corvale General, and Corvale Lakeside was inspected on 2023-02-03 and classified VAI, 12 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D7", "E17", "E1", "E4", "E7"]
    },
    {
      "text": "That same plant also received a VAI classification after an inspection ending 2023-04-21, 65 days after the posting.",
      "cites": ["D8", "E15"]
    },
    {
      "text": "An earlier inspection ending 2020-03-06 was classified VAI, 1,076 days before the posting.",
      "cites": ["D6", "E13"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hospira, Inc. plant that supplies the alternate manufacturer option was last inspected with an NAI classification on 2025-02-07.",
      "cites": ["E31"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East has 7.1 days of the 5 mL presentation on hand, Corvale Lakeside has 28.5 days, and Corvale General has 19.2 days.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D3", "D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule-based best option is to transfer 13 vials of the 10 mg/mL, 5 mL presentation from Corvale Lakeside to Corvale East, which would raise Corvale East to 9 days on hand while Corvale Lakeside retains two weeks of supply.",
      "cites": ["D10"]
    }
  ]
}
